    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the team with a 76.31 projection. His matchup against Roupp is bolstered by an elite batting order spot (#2) and a favorable platoon advantage. **Josh Naylor** also presents a strong 64.72 profile, primarily because he avoids the typical platoon penalty when facing a lefty like Kay, thanks to his high SP skill adjustment and advantageous spot in the heart of the order. **Austin Riley** is the surprise value play of the slate, sitting at 63.51; despite a neutral platoon, he is the primary beneficiary of facing Garrett, who carries a brutal 9.71 xERA, effectively neutralizing the park factor drawbacks for the 3B.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who landed at 39.37, just missing our 40.00 efficiency floor. While his base projection is solid, the combination of a daunting matchup against Suarez and a negative wind adjustment effectively stifled his scoring potential. Elsewhere, the lineup management continues to be constrained by our infirmary, with **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all remaining sidelined. We are keeping a close watch on **James Wood**; his 51.22 score is suppressed by facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm in McLean and a formidable catcher, but his top-of-the-order status keeps him in the lineup to hunt R and SB.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given our focus on the scarce SB category. **Brice Turang** earns a solid 56.74 despite the SP skill deficit because his matchup presents a prime opportunity for base thievery, and we have opted to start **Mickey Moniak** (60.43) despite the platoon disadvantage because the park factor provides a substantial +14% lift to his output. Managers should monitor any late-breaking weather patterns that might further degrade the scores for **Vinnie Pasquantino** should he be considered as a late pivot, and remain mindful that any shift in the batting order for **Gabriel Moreno**\u2014currently buried at #7\u2014could further dampen his efficiency.",
